-  <p>Il prodotto non dovrebbe richiedere categorie particolari di dati per le funzioni descritte; gli utenti non devono inserire dati sensibili nei link o nelle richieste di supporto. Questa frase e le istruzioni operative sono da verificare legalmente.</p>
+  <p>For click statistics, Brev stores only the referrer’s host, without its path, query parameters, credentials or fragment. No raw IP address or user agent is stored in click records. The user agent is reduced to <code>desktop</code>, <code>mobile</code>, <code>tablet</code> or <code>other</code>. The country comes from Cloudflare’s country header when available.</p>
+  <p>IP address and user agent are used only in memory to calculate a truncated HMAC-SHA256 visitor fingerprint. Its daily salt is derived from a server secret and the UTC date and is not stored. The fingerprint is non-reversible and cannot be linked across days. Repeat visits on the same link on the same day increase the count. Country, referrer host and device reflect that visitor’s first visit that day. Known robots and prefetch requests are excluded.</p>
+  <p>Visitor totals sum daily distinct visitors per link; they do not identify unique people across days or links. Visits without a calculable fingerprint count separately.</p>
+  <p>The described features should not require special categories of personal data. Users must not put sensitive data in links or support requests. This statement and operational guidance require legal review.</p>
 
-  <h2>5. Destinatari, responsabili e trasferimenti</h2>
-  <p>Per il futuro Cloud potranno essere coinvolti provider tecnici e responsabili del trattamento elencati nella pagina <a href="/subprocessors">Subprocessors &amp; Data Retention</a>. Stripe non è configurato nella configurazione corrente del repository; il provider email non è configurato di default. I nomi, i ruoli, i contratti, le garanzie e gli eventuali trasferimenti fuori dallo SEE sono <strong>[DA COMPLETARE]</strong>.</p>
-  <p>Prima del lancio devono essere verificati paesi di trattamento, sub-responsabili, SCC/altre garanzie quando necessarie, meccanismo informativo per le modifiche e procedura di notifica.</p>
+  <h2>5. Recipients, processors and transfers</h2>
+  <p>The future Cloud service may involve technical providers and processors listed on <a href="/subprocessors">Subprocessors &amp; Data Retention</a>. Stripe is not configured in the repository’s default configuration; neither is a transactional email provider. Names, roles, contracts, safeguards and any transfers outside the EEA are <strong>[DA COMPLETARE]</strong>.</p>
+  <p>Before launch, processing countries, subprocessors, SCCs or other safeguards where required, change notices and notification procedures must be verified.</p>
 
-  <h2>6. Conservazione</h2>
-  <p>Non sono indicati termini definitivi in questa bozza. Tempi per account, link, domini, contatori di click, sessioni/token, log di sicurezza, supporto e billing: <strong>[DA COMPLETARE - Matt e professionista legale devono definire tempi, criteri di cancellazione e possibili obblighi contabili/difensivi]</strong>.</p>
+  <h2>6. Retention</h2>
+  <p>Raw click events have a <strong>90-day retention policy by default</strong>, configurable by the self-hosted operator. Operators must apply this policy through regular pruning. Daily aggregates containing click counts and daily visitor counts are <strong>retained long term without automatic expiry</strong>, so historical totals survive pruning of raw events. Deleting a link deletes its click events and daily aggregates. Country, referrer and device breakdowns depend on retained raw events.</p>
+  <p>Retention and deletion criteria for accounts, links/domains, sessions/tokens, security logs, support and billing remain <strong>[DA COMPLETARE - Matt and a legal professional must confirm periods, deletion criteria and any accounting or legal obligations]</strong>. Backup and infrastructure-log retention must be confirmed separately.</p>
 
